1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;Because of Maren&amp;#39;s death during the journey&amp;nbsp; Jens and his son Hans Peter ( Rasmus&amp;#39; name is is not on the company lists or shipboard records so he may have come later) left Salt Lake afte
2 CONC r arriving there and went&amp;nbsp; directly to Sanpete.&amp;nbsp; When they arrived in Ephriam they found a city whose economy had been impacted by the&amp;nbsp;Black Hawk War.&amp;nbsp; Wheat was&amp;nbsp; five dollars per bushel and&amp;nbsp; fa
2 CONC rm labor paid&amp;nbsp; .25cents per day.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Because&amp;nbsp; Camp Douglas and Secretary of War refused to commit federal troups to defend settlers from Black Hawk it was necessary to form a Utah Territorial Militia.&amp;
2 CONC nbsp; Both Hans and Rasmus&amp;nbsp; enlisted for service in this militia and saw short term military service as a means&amp;nbsp; to earn a start in their new home&amp;nbsp; They served in a company commanded by Captain Lewis Larsen&amp;nbsp;. A b
2 CONC ill for maintaining the militia was submitted but never paid by the govenment so their pay was probably less than expected.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; All three received some land&amp;nbsp; and 1870 records show Jens Rassmussen&amp;nbsp; residin
2 CONC g within block 14 and Rasmus as a farmer living west of town.&amp;nbsp;The Census of 1880 shows Jens occupation was weaver and because there was no textile industry in Ephriam he may have woven and braided&amp;nbsp; items such as harness parts or r
2 CONC ugs from various materials.&amp;nbsp; Jens didnot remarry and&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; in 1880 was lliving with an illiterate male housekeeper from Sweden and his six year old daughter Botilda Olsen. Jens had abandoned church activity&amp;nbsp; after Ma
2 CONC ren&amp;#39;s death.&amp;nbsp; In 1885 he sold 5 lots to Rasmus for @@@@$200 each which was more than other comparable sales so&amp;nbsp; it probably provided for his subsistance until his death.&amp;nbsp; The marker for his grave in Ephriam pionee
2 CONC r cemetary has not survived.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
