2 CONC ;&gt;1735. Baltimore Co., MD.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Never married: (1) (1t) Will named daughter Elizabeth JOHNSON.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&amp;
2 CONC nbsp;- Death: (1) 1785. (1o) Was living 12 Sep 1784. (1t) Will dtd Nov 1772, probated 19 Mar 1787, Fayette Co., PA. (1) Fayette Co., PA.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font
2 CONC -size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;(1) &amp;nbsp;&quot;Christopher Gist of Maryland and Some of his descendants, 1679-1957,&quot; by Jean Muir Dorsey (Chicago, Ill., J.S. Swift Co., 1958; rpt. Heritage Quest online, 2009) p.13, 18, 28-29, 37, 50-54. C
2 CONC ites: (a) &quot;George Mercer Papers: Relating to the Ohio Company of Virginia,&quot; ed. Lois Mulkearn (Pittsburgh, 1954) p.172. &amp;nbsp;(b) &quot;The History of an Expedition Against Fort Dusquesne in 1755,&quot; by Winthrop Sargent, p.193-196
