1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;&amp;quot;&amp;quot;One of Absalom Boren&amp;#39;s fellow Morgan County farmers in 1830 was &amp;quot; Lawrance&amp;quot; Killebrew (1763-1835).&amp;nbsp; His father was Robert Killebrew (1730-1791).......The ev
2 CONC idence indicates that Lawrence Killebrew followed the same general migration pattern that Nicholas and Absalom Boren had taken.&amp;nbsp; In 1799 Lawrence was living in Kentucky, where his son William (1799-1881) was born.&amp;nbsp; Evidently Lawre
2 CONC nce and William came to the Illinois country together, arriving in present day Scott County, near the Illinois River, by 1828.&amp;nbsp; The older Killebrew died there in 1835.......; the Pike County Collector&amp;#39;s book lists William Killebre
2 CONC w as the owner of 381 acres in Montezuma Township.&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
