2 TITL Will of William Kylburn 1500
1 _OID e5e0c4eb-6482-4c48-9605-d32f804d5e79
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;A.D. 1500 - Will of WILLIAM KYLBURN, of Cambridgeshire, copied from the Registry of the Bishop of Ely:&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&quot;In dei noie Amen, the xiiijth day of February An&amp;deg; dn 1&amp;deg
2 CONC ; five c, I WILm. KYLBURN, makythe my testament In thys man.&lt;br&gt;I commend my sawll to Alymyghty God.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;Item. I bequay to the hight Auter vjviijd.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;It. To the repar
2 CONC acon off the chyrche vjs viijd.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;It. To my Viff a cowe and scheppe and other stoffe to the valeur off xls wt.&amp;nbsp; All seche goods as sche haud hir Awn at the ty of AurMarage and Also my best brass pot s
2 CONC awy an.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;It. I bequeth to John my eldyst son my copy holds In wiche John Mauning nowe dweleth wt the lands app&apos;tnyng thereto.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;It. I bequeth to Thom. my son my ten
2 CONC ements wt the croft and and app&apos;rtinanc In wich Andrew Salew&apos;n dewylleth And All the Wood app&apos;tenyg y&apos; to, I beqewth to Wilm. my son except frut trees.&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;It. I beqweth to the sayd Thom. th
2 CONC e two oxen and my best schod cart.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;It. To the sayd Wilm. two oxen and my other schod cartt and to them two a bowd cawdron.&lt;br&gt;It. To Agnes my dawther vj colmes malt, A cowe and my gret almery wt my best brass pot.&lt;br&gt;
2 CONC It. To Margrete my dowther iiij colmes barly and a black cow calff wt a posnyg.&lt;br&gt;It. To Elisab. my doght. one colme barly wyd wt my wite pay&apos;.&lt;br&gt;It. To Johanne my doght. an hakfer wt a white face.&lt;br&gt;It. To my sonnes Rob
2 CONC . Hugh and Nicholas to ev&apos;y of them a colme malt.&lt;br&gt;It. I beqwethe to my said sonnes John, Thos. and Wilm. the terme of yeres wich I have in my ferme at Trompy&apos;ton both In the man&apos; and that I have wt John gardea&apos; wt thy
2 CONC s condicon yt they shall wt the profetts fo the same ber all chargys and frely send both mete and drynck and clothe ther brother and syster unto the time they be abyll to helppe them selffe.&amp;nbsp; And when my sayd childer to be off lawfull Ag
2 CONC e and discrecion than I wyll yat my executors delyv&apos; to ev&apos; of thame there legats or els the walews y&apos;off and iff eny of thame dye wyth In age his part so deed be devarded according to Resen that he so mysruled by the discecon of m
2 CONC y sead executors be adwodye fro&apos; the co&apos;paney.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;The residew of my goods I beqweth to the sayd John my sen sonne and to Wilm Bradlay whom I make my executors And Andrew Kylborn my brother ov&apos;see
2 CONC r.&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&quot;Whytness the curat the sayd Andrew John Let&apos; and oder yeme at compynes daye yere A bowth sayd.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
